1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,471
It's New Year's Eve.

2
00:00:01,371 --> 00:00:03,774
Your friends are making big promises again.

3
00:00:03,974 --> 00:00:05,268
New gym. New diet.

4
00:00:05,168 --> 00:00:06,861
This is finally my year.

5
00:00:07,211 --> 00:00:08,741
And you? You're just smiling.

6
00:00:08,941 --> 00:00:10,064
Because one year ago,

7
00:00:09,964 --> 00:00:11,867
you made a different kind of promise.

8
00:00:12,217 --> 00:00:13,575
Not one big change.

9
00:00:13,475 --> 00:00:14,568
Ten small ones.

10
00:00:14,768 --> 00:00:16,567
So small they almost felt silly.

11
00:00:16,917 --> 00:00:19,326
Tonight, your savings account says five thousand

12
00:00:19,226 --> 00:00:21,347
three hundred dollars more than last year.

13
00:00:21,547 --> 00:00:23,229
And your life feels calmer than it

14
00:00:23,129 --> 00:00:23,834
has in years.

15
00:00:24,184 --> 00:00:26,250
Meanwhile, Jake just checked his card.

16
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:28,449
He spent more on holiday gifts than

17
00:00:28,349 --> 00:00:29,425
he has in savings.

18
00:00:29,775 --> 00:00:31,674
Here are the ten small things you

19
00:00:31,574 --> 00:00:34,126
did. And exactly how much each one was worth.

20
00:00:34,476 --> 00:00:36,746
Thing number one. You paid yourself first.

21
00:00:36,946 --> 00:00:39,872
Fifty dollars, moved automatically to savings,

22
00:00:39,772 --> 00:00:40,978
every single week.

23
00:00:41,328 --> 00:00:42,656
You never saw that money,

24
00:00:42,556 --> 00:00:43,785
so you never missed it.

25
00:00:43,985 --> 00:00:47,028
By December, that alone was twenty six hundred dollars.

26
00:00:47,378 --> 00:00:49,112
Thing number two. Every Sunday,

27
00:00:49,012 --> 00:00:51,116
five minutes. You opened your bank app

28
00:00:51,016 --> 00:00:51,959
and just looked.

29
00:00:52,159 --> 00:00:53,883
No judging. Just looking.

30
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:56,642
Most people avoid that app when money is tight.

31
00:00:56,842 --> 00:00:58,762
Mia hadn't opened hers in two months.

32
00:00:59,112 --> 00:01:01,532
Thing number three. The twenty four hour rule.

33
00:01:01,732 --> 00:01:03,879
Anything you want that costs over fifty

34
00:01:03,779 --> 00:01:05,244
dollars, you wait one day.

35
00:01:05,594 --> 00:01:07,257
Half the time, the next morning,

36
00:01:07,157 --> 00:01:08,820
you didn't even want it anymore.

37
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:10,746
Jake has a different rule.

38
00:01:10,646 --> 00:01:11,598
See it, buy it.

39
00:01:11,798 --> 00:01:13,578
His closet is full of things with

40
00:01:13,478 --> 00:01:14,494
the tags still on.

41
00:01:14,844 --> 00:01:16,840
Thing number four. You cooked dinner at

42
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:18,298
home three more nights a week.

43
00:01:18,648 --> 00:01:20,971
A delivery dinner was costing you around

44
00:01:20,871 --> 00:01:23,361
twenty five dollars. Cooking it, about ten.

45
00:01:23,561 --> 00:01:25,564
Fifteen dollars saved each time.

46
00:01:25,464 --> 00:01:27,525
Over two thousand dollars a year.

47
00:01:27,875 --> 00:01:30,574
Thing number five. You canceled two subscriptions

48
00:01:30,474 --> 00:01:31,581
you forgot you had.

49
00:01:31,781 --> 00:01:33,093
Thirty dollars a month.

50
00:01:32,993 --> 00:01:34,146
Gone in ten minutes.

51
00:01:34,496 --> 00:01:37,221
Thing number six. One no spend day every week.

52
00:01:37,421 --> 00:01:39,208
Wednesdays. No coffee shop.

53
00:01:39,108 --> 00:01:40,832
No online orders. Nothing.

54
00:01:41,182 --> 00:01:43,701
It sounds tiny. But it taught you something big.

55
00:01:43,901 --> 00:01:46,262
Most of your spending was habit, not need.

56
00:01:46,612 --> 00:01:48,851
Thing number seven. You paid your credit

57
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:50,242
card in full. Every month.

58
00:01:50,442 --> 00:01:53,118
Card interest often runs over twenty percent

59
00:01:53,018 --> 00:01:54,406
a year. You paid zero.

60
00:01:54,756 --> 00:01:56,027
Mia pays the minimum.

61
00:01:56,227 --> 00:01:58,176
Her balance hasn't moved all year,

62
00:01:58,076 --> 00:01:59,972
even though she pays every month.

63
00:02:00,322 --> 00:02:02,558
Thing number eight. Ten pages a day.

64
00:02:02,758 --> 00:02:03,886
Not a book a week.

65
00:02:03,786 --> 00:02:06,112
Just ten pages, every night before bed.

66
00:02:06,462 --> 00:02:08,602
That's over three thousand pages in a

67
00:02:08,502 --> 00:02:10,256
year. More than a dozen books.

68
00:02:10,456 --> 00:02:12,115
A few of them were about money.

69
00:02:12,015 --> 00:02:13,473
They changed how you think.

70
00:02:13,823 --> 00:02:16,175
Thing number nine. A twenty minute walk,

71
00:02:16,075 --> 00:02:17,976
every day. Phone in your pocket.

72
00:02:18,326 --> 00:02:20,221
You slept better. You stressed less.

73
00:02:20,421 --> 00:02:22,146
And stressed people spend more.

74
00:02:22,046 --> 00:02:23,456
That's not a coincidence.

75
00:02:23,806 --> 00:02:25,526
Thing number ten. The big one.

76
00:02:25,426 --> 00:02:27,093
When you got a raise in June,

77
00:02:26,993 --> 00:02:28,227
you saved half of it.

78
00:02:28,577 --> 00:02:30,352
You still enjoyed the other half.

79
00:02:30,252 --> 00:02:32,890
But your lifestyle didn't jump with your paycheck.

80
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,565
Jake got a raise too.

81
00:02:34,465 --> 00:02:36,841
A week later, he had a new car payment.

82
00:02:37,191 --> 00:02:39,651
Here's what nobody tells you about small things.

83
00:02:39,851 --> 00:02:41,923
On their own, they don't feel like anything.

84
00:02:42,273 --> 00:02:44,548
Fifty dollars doesn't feel like much.

85
00:02:44,448 --> 00:02:46,487
Ten pages doesn't feel like much.

86
00:02:46,687 --> 00:02:48,967
But they stack. Every day. Every week.

87
00:02:49,317 --> 00:02:52,329
Big resolutions fail because they need motivation.

88
00:02:52,529 --> 00:02:54,544
Small habits work because they don't.

89
00:02:54,894 --> 00:02:55,874
Let's add it up.

90
00:02:56,074 --> 00:02:59,004
Fifty a week. Cooking at home. Two subscriptions.

91
00:02:59,354 --> 00:03:01,294
That's about fifty three hundred dollars.

92
00:03:01,494 --> 00:03:03,346
And that's before the money you didn't

93
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:05,052
waste on things you'd have regretted.

94
00:03:05,402 --> 00:03:07,429
Put that in a high yield savings

95
00:03:07,329 --> 00:03:09,296
account, and it can even earn a

96
00:03:09,196 --> 00:03:11,102
bit of interest. Rates change,

97
00:03:11,002 --> 00:03:12,427
nothing is guaranteed.

98
00:03:12,627 --> 00:03:14,333
But the real win isn't the money.

99
00:03:14,683 --> 00:03:15,665
It's the feeling.

100
00:03:15,865 --> 00:03:18,004
When your car needed new tires in

101
00:03:17,904 --> 00:03:19,981
October, you just paid for them.

102
00:03:19,881 --> 00:03:21,093
No panic. No card.

103
00:03:21,443 --> 00:03:22,477
Back at the party,

104
00:03:22,377 --> 00:03:23,981
Jake asks you how you did it.

105
00:03:24,181 --> 00:03:25,514
Did you get a big raise?

106
00:03:25,864 --> 00:03:27,140
You laugh. Not really.

107
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,733
I just did ten small things. Every day.

108
00:03:30,083 --> 00:03:31,333
So here's your plan.

109
00:03:31,233 --> 00:03:32,886
Don't try all ten tomorrow.

110
00:03:33,086 --> 00:03:35,113
Pick two. The two that feel easiest.

111
00:03:35,463 --> 00:03:37,740
My pick? Set up the automatic transfer

112
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,802
tonight. Even twenty dollars a week.

113
00:03:40,002 --> 00:03:41,522
And put a twenty four hour rule

114
00:03:41,422 --> 00:03:42,529
on your shopping cart.

115
00:03:42,879 --> 00:03:45,020
Next month, add one more. Then another.

116
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:46,533
By next New Year's Eve,

117
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:48,009
you won't need a resolution.

118
00:03:48,359 --> 00:03:50,677
You'll be the one smiling quietly at the party.

119
00:03:51,027 --> 00:03:53,013
If this helped, subscribe for a new

120
00:03:52,913 --> 00:03:54,523
simple money move every day.

121
00:03:54,723 --> 00:03:56,136
And tell me in the comments.

122
00:03:56,036 --> 00:03:58,294
Which of the ten things are you starting with?
